<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Groups</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>group</a>
group &lt;character&gt;
</pre>
<p>Groups are good to have if you want to go on a big adventure: they are often 
safer, as you are protected by the other members.
</p><p>To form a group, first decide who is to be the leader; the leader is going to 
get beaten up the most, so make a good choice. Each one who wants to join must 
follow the leader (see <a cmd='#'>Help Follow</a>). That alone doesn't make them part of the 
group: the leader then makes each follower a member, like group asta. To put a 
member out of the group, the leader types the same again; to stop them 
following too, ditch them. group alone shows who is in your group.
</p><p>When the group kills something, everyone in the group who is there gets a share 
of the experience. Each share is smaller the more you are, but together you get 
more than one player alone would. The shares are measured against the highest 
level in the group, so a member far below the others gets less.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Follow</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ditch</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Assist</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Split</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Experience</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Group Teleport</a>
</pre>




</div>